From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:35:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 48/60] perf(canvas): no live documents before a page's camera
 first rests

Until a page's camera first rests it is about to be fitted or put back
where it was, and the view it has is the last page's (on a first load,
100% at the origin). The culling effect booted documents for that view
at once, before the fit effect moved the camera, and tore them down at
the rest. Each is a sandboxed iframe whose creation blocks the main
thread (an out-of-process frame: createChildframe, insertBefore and a
sync IPC).

Traced first load of a 459-frame canvas: two documents made and removed
in the task that took the canvas in, about 350 ms at full CPU and 1.7 s
at a 4x CPU slowdown. Now only the pinned documents boot before the
first rest, and the load makes no iframe it throws away.
---
 src/components/Stage.tsx | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/components/Stage.tsx b/src/components/Stage.tsx
index 2fa9bc9..62a5ec8 100644
--- a/src/components/Stage.tsx
+++ b/src/components/Stage.tsx
@@ -580,7 +580,14 @@ export function Stage({
       const live = useLiveFrames.getState()
       const stage = measuredStage(el)
       if (rested) live.setPreviews(s.viewport.zoom * window.devicePixelRatio, sharpPreviews(frames, s.viewport, stage))
-      admit(computeLiveFrames(frames, s.viewport, stage, pinned, live.ids ?? new Set()), pinned)
+      const wanted = computeLiveFrames(frames, s.viewport, stage, pinned, live.ids ?? new Set())
+      /* Until a new page's camera first rests it is about to be fitted or put
+         back where it was, and the view it has is the last page's (on a first
+         load, 100% at the origin). Documents booted for that view are torn
+         down at the rest: each is a sandboxed iframe whose creation blocks the
+         main thread (a large canvas's first load made two, ~350 ms, in the
+         task that took the canvas in). So until then only the pinned boot. */
+      admit(rested ? wanted : new Set([...wanted].filter((id) => pinned.has(id))), pinned)
     }
     function atRest() {
       rested = true
